  "name_sub": "you, the tractor maker",
  "description": "You are Ferruccio Lamborghini. Your name is on 10,687 supercars a year. And it all started with a tractor.\n\nSources:\n- Wikipedia: Ferruccio Lamborghini: https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Ferruccio_Lamborghini\n- Wikipedia: Lamborghini: https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Lamborghini\n\nFrom the cited pages: Ferruccio Lamborghini was born in 1916 to grape farmers in Renazzo di Cento, Italy; after the war he built tractors from leftover military engines and parts and founded Lamborghini Trattori in 1948, which quickly became an important maker of farm machines; in 1958 he bought a Ferrari 250 GT whose clutch kept failing; he raised it with Enzo Ferrari and was dismissed (in his own later telling, Ferrari called him a tractor maker; Wikipedia notes the story is as much legend as fact); he founded Automobili Lamborghini in 1963 and chose a raging bull as its badge after visiting a Spanish fighting-bull ranch in 1962; the 1966 Miura used a rear mid-engine layout; in 1971 big tractor orders were cancelled and in 1972 he sold the tractor company to SAME; he sold 51% of the car company to Georges-Henri Rossetti for US$600,000; the car company went bankrupt in 1978, changed owners several times and was sold to the Volkswagen Group (under Audi) in 1998; he retired to an estate in Umbria and made wine. Lamborghini built 10,687 vehicles and had €3.10 billion in revenue in 2024. Not financial advice.\n\n#shorts #lamborghini #ferrari #howtheymakemoney",
